    <subfield code="a">Travel guide series</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A tunnel book.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book shows a view of the city of Florence from the steps of the church of San Miniato al Monte. The images were painted on Muirhead's Blue Guides and Baedeker's travel guide pages published in the 1920's. It is the first in a series of books that incorporates old travel guidebooks and maps."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Images were painted directly on guidebook pages, then offset printed and accordian bound on sides by hand.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Davidson writes that she chose this format to reproduce an effect of real distance and space.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited ed. of 500.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC has copy no. 175 signed by the artist.</subfield>
